{"id":"e50619e8ca5f10b0","group":"17","path":"17/17-df-partial-type-boolean-operations.md","title":"Boolean Combination of Partial Types","display":"df-partial-type-boolean-operations — Boolean Combination of Partial Types","type":"definition","metadata":{"numbering_status":"local atom identifier; not the book result number","source_verification":"pending exact book correspondence; local formulation reviewed, not source-verified","type":"definition","book":"Model Theory (Chang & Keisler, 3rd ed. 1990)","book_abbrev":"17","label":"17-df-partial-type-boolean-operations","aliases":["17-df-partial-type-boolean-operations"],"display":"df-partial-type-boolean-operations — Boolean Combination of Partial Types","depends_on":["[[17-df-type]]","[[17-df-symbols]]","[[17-df-ordinals-finiteness]]","[[17-df-symbol-alphabet]]","[[17-df-linear-order]]"],"label_origin":"local-catalog","legacy_label":"17-df-6.3.2b","local_revision":"content audit of supplied 17(1).zip; inherited source_verification and bibliographic fields not independently reverified"},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"numbering_status","html":"local atom identifier; not the book result number"},{"key":"source_verification","html":"pending exact book correspondence; local formulation reviewed, not source-verified"},{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Model Theory (Chang &amp; Keisler, 3rd ed. 1990)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"17"},{"key":"label","html":"17-df-partial-type-boolean-operations"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>17-df-partial-type-boolean-operations</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-partial-type-boolean-operations — Boolean Combination of Partial Types"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"07adad8c036296f7\" href=\"?note=07adad8c036296f7\" title=\"17-df-type\">17-df-type</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"3eb5325f08c84582\" href=\"?note=3eb5325f08c84582\" title=\"17-df-symbols\">17-df-symbols</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"b6e4a36b436c9b93\" href=\"?note=b6e4a36b436c9b93\" title=\"17-df-ordinals-finiteness\">17-df-ordinals-finiteness</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"058f3c1c00535492\" href=\"?note=058f3c1c00535492\" title=\"17-df-symbol-alphabet\">17-df-symbol-alphabet</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"3f12d30db6793ecd\" href=\"?note=3f12d30db6793ecd\" title=\"17-df-linear-order\">17-df-linear-order</a></span></div>"},{"key":"label_origin","html":"local-catalog"},{"key":"legacy_label","html":"17-df-6.3.2b"},{"key":"local_revision","html":"content audit of supplied 17(1).zip; inherited source_verification and bibliographic fields not independently reverified"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\\in\\mathrm{FirstOrderLanguages}\">\\(L\\in\\mathrm{FirstOrderLanguages}\\)</span>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\triangleleft\\subseteq\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}\\times\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}\">\\(\\triangleleft\\subseteq\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}\\times\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}\\)</span>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{WellOrder}(\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n},\\triangleleft)\">\\(\\operatorname{WellOrder}(\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n},\\triangleleft)\\)</span>，见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"3f12d30db6793ecd\" href=\"?note=3f12d30db6793ecd\" title=\"17-df-linear-order\">17-df-linear-order</a>；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"e\">\\(e\\)</span> 为候选集合函数。</p>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\in\\omega\">\\(n\\in\\omega\\)</span>; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p,q\\subseteq\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}\">\\(p,q\\subseteq\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}\\)</span> (formula families, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"07adad8c036296f7\" href=\"?note=07adad8c036296f7\" title=\"17-df-type\">17-df-type</a>).</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\triangleleft\">\\(\\triangleleft\\)</span> is a fixed well-order of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}\">\\(\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}\\)</span>; Boolean syntax is from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"3eb5325f08c84582\" href=\"?note=3eb5325f08c84582\" title=\"17-df-symbols\">17-df-symbols</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Finite}\">\\(\\mathrm{Finite}\\)</span> (finite-set predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-9\" data-note=\"b6e4a36b436c9b93\" href=\"?note=b6e4a36b436c9b93\" title=\"17-df-ordinals-finiteness\">17-df-ordinals-finiteness</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\sqcap,\\sqcup\">\\(\\sqcap,\\sqcup\\)</span> are operations on formula families. <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Enum}_{\\triangleleft}\">\\(\\operatorname{Enum}_{\\triangleleft}\\)</span> has domain the finite formula families and returns their increasing enumeration; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"C_n\">\\(C_n\\)</span> has domain <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}^{&lt;\\omega}\">\\(\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}^{&lt;\\omega}\\)</span>; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Neg}_{\\triangleleft}\">\\(\\operatorname{Neg}_{\\triangleleft}\\)</span> has domain the finite formula families and returns a singleton formula family. These operations are defined here by the displayed graph and recursion.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\quad\np\\sqcap q\n&amp;=p\\cup q,\\\\\np\\sqcup q\n&amp;=\\{\\varphi\\lor\\psi:\\varphi\\in p,\\ \\psi\\in q\\},\\\\\n\\mathrm{Finite}(p)&amp;\\to\n\\left[\\operatorname{Enum}_{\\triangleleft}(p)=e\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists m\\in\\omega\\;(\\operatorname{Bij}(e,m,p)\\land\n\\forall i,j&lt;m\\;(i&lt;j\\to e(i)\\triangleleft e(j)))\\right],\\\\\nC_n(\\langle\\rangle)&amp;=\\forall x_0\\,(\\operatorname{lit}(x_0)=\\operatorname{lit}(x_0)),\\\\\nC_n(s\\mathbin{{}^\\frown}\\langle\\varphi\\rangle)&amp;=(C_n(s)\\land\\varphi)\n\\quad(s\\in\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}^{&lt;\\omega},\\ \\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}),\\\\\n\\mathrm{Finite}(p)&amp;\\to\n\\operatorname{Neg}_{\\triangleleft}(p)\n=\\{\\neg C_n(\\operatorname{Enum}_{\\triangleleft}(p))\\}.\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\quad\np\\sqcap q\n&amp;=p\\cup q,\\\\\np\\sqcup q\n&amp;=\\{\\varphi\\lor\\psi:\\varphi\\in p,\\ \\psi\\in q\\},\\\\\n\\mathrm{Finite}(p)&amp;\\to\n\\left[\\operatorname{Enum}_{\\triangleleft}(p)=e\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists m\\in\\omega\\;(\\operatorname{Bij}(e,m,p)\\land\n\\forall i,j&lt;m\\;(i&lt;j\\to e(i)\\triangleleft e(j)))\\right],\\\\\nC_n(\\langle\\rangle)&amp;=\\forall x_0\\,(\\operatorname{lit}(x_0)=\\operatorname{lit}(x_0)),\\\\\nC_n(s\\mathbin{{}^\\frown}\\langle\\varphi\\rangle)&amp;=(C_n(s)\\land\\varphi)\n\\quad(s\\in\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}^{&lt;\\omega},\\ \\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}),\\\\\n\\mathrm{Finite}(p)&amp;\\to\n\\operatorname{Neg}_{\\triangleleft}(p)\n=\\{\\neg C_n(\\operatorname{Enum}_{\\triangleleft}(p))\\}.\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>Realizing <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p\\sqcap q\">\\(p\\sqcap q\\)</span> means realizing both families, while realizing\n<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p\\sqcup q\">\\(p\\sqcup q\\)</span> means realizing at least one of them.  For an infinite partial type,\nthe complement of its realization set need not be represented by a single\npartial type; in particular <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\{\\neg\\varphi:\\varphi\\in p\\}\">\\(\\{\\neg\\varphi:\\varphi\\in p\\}\\)</span> is generally not the\nnegation of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p\">\\(p\\)</span>.</p>\n<p>The fixed well-order removes the syntactic ordering ambiguity of a conjunction indexed by a finite set. Finite increasing enumerations are unique, and recursion on the sequence length defines <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"C_n\">\\(C_n\\)</span> uniquely. Its empty value is a sentence, so even <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n=0\">\\(n=0\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p=\\varnothing\">\\(p=\\varnothing\\)</span> remain well typed. Negation returns a formula family and realizes exactly the complement of realizing <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p\">\\(p\\)</span>; the well-order affects its syntax, not its truth conditions.</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"17-df-type","status":"resolved","id":"07adad8c036296f7","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[17-df-type]]","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-symbols","status":"resolved","id":"3eb5325f08c84582","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[17-df-symbols]]","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-ordinals-finiteness","status":"resolved","id":"b6e4a36b436c9b93","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[17-df-ordinals-finiteness]]","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-symbol-alphabet","status":"resolved","id":"058f3c1c00535492","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[17-df-symbol-alphabet]]","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-linear-order","status":"resolved","id":"3f12d30db6793ecd","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[17-df-linear-order]]","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-linear-order","status":"resolved","id":"3f12d30db6793ecd","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$L\\in\\mathrm{FirstOrderLanguages}$，$\\triangleleft\\subseteq\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}\\times\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}$，$\\operatorname{WellOrder}(\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n},\\triangleleft)$，见 [[17-df-linear-order]]；$e$ 为候选集合函数。","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-type","status":"resolved","id":"07adad8c036296f7","anchor":"ref-7","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$n\\in\\omega$; $p,q\\subseteq\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}$ (formula families, see [[17-df-type]]).","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-symbols","status":"resolved","id":"3eb5325f08c84582","anchor":"ref-8","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\triangleleft$ is a fixed well-order of $\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}$; Boolean syntax is from [[17-df-symbols]].","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-ordinals-finiteness","status":"resolved","id":"b6e4a36b436c9b93","anchor":"ref-9","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Finite}$ (finite-set predicate, see [[17-df-ordinals-finiteness]])","embed":false}],"attachments":[],"math":[{"tex":"L\\in\\mathrm{FirstOrderLanguages}","display":false},{"tex":"\\triangleleft\\subseteq\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}\\times\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{WellOrder}(\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n},\\triangleleft)","display":false},{"tex":"e","display":false},{"tex":"n\\in\\omega","display":false},{"tex":"p,q\\subseteq\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}","display":false},{"tex":"\\triangleleft","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Finite}","display":false},{"tex":"\\sqcap,\\sqcup","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{Enum}_{\\triangleleft}","display":false},{"tex":"C_n","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}^{<\\omega}","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{Neg}_{\\triangleleft}","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\quad\np\\sqcap q\n&=p\\cup q,\\\\\np\\sqcup q\n&=\\{\\varphi\\lor\\psi:\\varphi\\in p,\\ \\psi\\in q\\},\\\\\n\\mathrm{Finite}(p)&\\to\n\\left[\\operatorname{Enum}_{\\triangleleft}(p)=e\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists m\\in\\omega\\;(\\operatorname{Bij}(e,m,p)\\land\n\\forall i,j<m\\;(i<j\\to e(i)\\triangleleft e(j)))\\right],\\\\\nC_n(\\langle\\rangle)&=\\forall x_0\\,(\\operatorname{lit}(x_0)=\\operatorname{lit}(x_0)),\\\\\nC_n(s\\mathbin{{}^\\frown}\\langle\\varphi\\rangle)&=(C_n(s)\\land\\varphi)\n\\quad(s\\in\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}^{<\\omega},\\ \\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}),\\\\\n\\mathrm{Finite}(p)&\\to\n\\operatorname{Neg}_{\\triangleleft}(p)\n=\\{\\neg C_n(\\operatorname{Enum}_{\\triangleleft}(p))\\}.\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"p\\sqcap q","display":false},{"tex":"p\\sqcup q","display":false},{"tex":"\\{\\neg\\varphi:\\varphi\\in p\\}","display":false},{"tex":"p","display":false},{"tex":"C_n","display":false},{"tex":"n=0","display":false},{"tex":"p=\\varnothing","display":false},{"tex":"p","display":false}],"bytes":3257,"backlinks":[{"id":"13c73c6f79ee78a7","anchor":"ref-74","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[17-df-partial-type-boolean-operations]]"},{"id":"2c98c9e634ff4b44","anchor":"ref-90","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[17-df-abstract-logic]]\n[[17-df-abstract-logic-compactness]]\n[[17-df-abstract-logic-lowenheim-skolem]]\n[[17-df-aleph-one-categoricity]]\n[[17-df-aleph-zero-categoricity]]\n[[17-df-algebraic-closure]]\n[[17-df-assignment]]\n[[17-df-assignment-predicate]]\n[[17-df-atomic-formula]]\n[[17-df-atomic-model]]\n[[17-df-atomic-model-notation]]\n[[17-df-bool-comb]]\n[[17-df-boolean-algebra]]\n[[17-df-boolean-valued-expansion]]\n[[17-df-boolean-valued-relation]]\n[[17-df-bound-variable]]\n[[17-df-cardinal-arithmetic]]\n[[17-df-cardinal-saturation]]\n[[17-df-categoricity]]\n[[17-df-chain-union]]\n[[17-df-chain-union-preservation]]\n[[17-df-complete-formula]]\n[[17-df-deduction-system]]\n[[17-df-definable-closure]]\n[[17-df-definable-set]]\n[[17-df-dense-linear-order]]\n[[17-df-diagram]]\n[[17-df-elementary-amalgamation]]\n[[17-df-elementary-amalgamat